Project: Django. Upgrade: 3.2 -> 4.2. Release of these items: 4.0.
Source: Django 4.0 release notes.

Label every item:
- risk = the change could break an application or deployment, require migration work, or create operational risk for SOME user upgrading across this release (removed or renamed APIs/settings/flags, changed defaults, behavior changes, raised minimum versions of runtimes/databases/dependencies, data or schema migration, required config changes, deprecated-and-removed features).
- context = accurate and useful but needs no user action at this release: explicitly "no user action required", a deprecation that still works (warning only), a purely additive new feature or option, documentation pointers.
- noise = credits, install/download commands, pure bug fixes that cannot change correct behavior, marketing text, headings with no content.

Return one label per item_id with a one-sentence reason grounded in the item text.

Items (JSON lines):
{"item_id": "5f228083c6d4", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / django.contrib.gis", "text": "Added support for SpatiaLite 5."}
{"item_id": "4145706b9cfc", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / django.contrib.gis", "text": "GDALRaster now allows creating rasters in any GDAL virtual filesystem."}
{"item_id": "bd70e4b5b3e9", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / django.contrib.gis", "text": "The new GISModelAdmin class allows customizing the widget used for GeometryField. This is encouraged instead of deprecated GeoModelAdmin and OSMGeoAdmin."}
{"item_id": "d009435c5616", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / django.contrib.postgres", "text": "The PostgreSQL backend now supports connecting by a service name. See postgresql-connection-settings for more details."}
{"item_id": "ffdccb4536d4", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / django.contrib.postgres", "text": "The new AddConstraintNotValid operation allows creating check constraints on PostgreSQL without verifying that all existing rows satisfy the new constraint."}
{"item_id": "02ed17f5128d", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / django.contrib.postgres", "text": "The new ValidateConstraint operation allows validating check constraints which were created using AddConstraintNotValid on PostgreSQL."}
{"item_id": "7418aa16aa66", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / django.contrib.postgres", "text": "The new ArraySubquery() expression allows using subqueries to construct lists of values on PostgreSQL."}
{"item_id": "16ca3bddc6f4", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / django.contrib.postgres", "text": "The new trigram_word_similar lookup, and the TrigramWordDistance() and TrigramWordSimilarity() expressions allow using trigram word similarity."}
{"item_id": "78fdb5d1263d", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / django.contrib.staticfiles", "text": "ManifestStaticFilesStorage now replaces paths to JavaScript source map references with their hashed counterparts."}
{"item_id": "cba58d40bc99", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / django.contrib.staticfiles", "text": "The new manifest_storage argument of ManifestFilesMixin and ManifestStaticFilesStorage allows customizing the manifest file storage."}
{"item_id": "da4b970c4af9", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Cache", "text": "The new async API for django.core.cache.backends.base.BaseCache begins the process of making cache backends async-compatible. The new async methods all have a prefixed names, e.g. aadd(), aget(), aset(), aget_or_set(), or adelete_many(). Going forward, the a prefix will be used for async variants of methods generally."}
{"item_id": "a74c86e31c55", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / CSRF", "text": "CSRF protection now consults the Origin header, if present. To facilitate this, some changes to the CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS setting are required."}
{"item_id": "746f811b09bd", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Forms", "text": "ModelChoiceField now includes the provided value in the params argument of a raised ValidationError for the invalid_choice error message. This allows custom error messages to use the %(value)s placeholder."}
{"item_id": "7043b47ce6cd", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Forms", "text": "BaseFormSet now renders non-form errors with an additional class of nonform to help distinguish them from form-specific errors."}
{"item_id": "2e1cc39a11aa", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Forms", "text": "BaseFormSet now allows customizing the widget used when deleting forms via can_delete by setting the deletion_widget attribute or overriding get_deletion_widget method."}
{"item_id": "bb08a0b5e7e7", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Internationalization", "text": "Added support and translations for the Malay language."}
{"item_id": "cc7d5129b958", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Generic Views", "text": "DeleteView now uses FormMixin, allowing you to provide a Form subclass, with a checkbox for example, to confirm deletion. In addition, this allows DeleteView to function with django.contrib.messages.views.SuccessMessageMixin. In accordance with FormMixin, object deletion for POST requests is handled in form_valid(). Custom delete logic in delete() handlers should be moved to form_valid(), or a shared helper method, as needed."}
{"item_id": "5d4fd50e8c14", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Logging", "text": "The alias of the database used in an SQL call is now passed as extra context along with each message to the django-db-logger logger."}
{"item_id": "25892f373a84", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Management Commands", "text": "The runserver management command now supports the --skip-checks option."}
{"item_id": "4c02e8d27910", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Management Commands", "text": "On PostgreSQL, dbshell now supports specifying a password file."}
